From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:24:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Hand the files out by signed URLs

Another service takes the board's files: a frontend's download links, or
a service that reads them. Through board_file, each request comes
through the app, with a sign-in. A signed URL serves one file to
whoever has it, until it ends, with no sign-in: on S3 straight from the
bucket.

- api_board_files, GET /api/boards/{id}/files, staff only: each file's
  Name, Type, Size and URL. The URL is maago.MediaURL(ctx, f.media(),
  time.Hour), made after the check: whoever gets it gets the file, so
  the view checks who asks before it makes any. An hour is enough for
  one download, and it ends long before the 7 days a URL may last
- A local store makes its URLs from its SiteURL, the site's address
  with the prefix: main gives LocalMedia SiteURL: auth.SiteURL + "/app".
  Handler refuses a SiteURL whose path is not Config.Prefix. A local
  URL is served by the process that made it, and no longer once it
  starts again: one machine's files, one process's URLs. A bucket's
  URLs are the bucket's

TestFileURLs serves the app on an httptest server whose address is the
store's SiteURL, asks for the list with staff's token, and downloads
the file by its URL with no sign-in. The tests' store has a SiteURL
now; TestUnderApp's has /app in it, as its Prefix.

